#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""scaling_4x3.py: the 4x3 scaling figure of the evaluation: new unique region paths found over the exploration time of one check on 1, 2, 4 and 8 machines; one
column per system (HDFS, ZooKeeper, HBase, Solr), three checks per system, so 12 panels and 48 lines.

    python3 scaling_4x3.py            writes scaling-4x3.pdf and scaling-4x3.png next to this file (needs matplotlib and numpy)
    python3 scaling_4x3.py PREFIX     writes PREFIX.pdf and PREFIX.png

Every number is in this file (DATA): per panel and machine count, the plotted line sampled every 5 seconds, as the figure shows it. These lines were produced by
reproduce/ on the experiment branch of JHSUYU/GraphChecker (reproduce.sh, from the kept traces of the runs; commit a2cc35943), which counts each run's unique
region paths under the system's rule (HDFS F7t4, ZooKeeper W, HBase F1, Solr W), lets the runs of a panel that reached their fixed point inside the window end on the paths all of them found,
and smooths each line by a Gaussian of 5 % of the panel's width. That folder has the traces, the counting rules and the per-run numbers; this script only draws.

Per run, in RUNS: how it stopped (FIXED_POINT: it ran out of worlds; LIMIT: its time limit; PLANNER_HEAP_EXCEEDED: the planner's heap filled), its sessions, and the
paths it had found at the window's end. Windows: HDFS, HBase and Solr panels show 45 minutes of exploration, ZooKeeper panels 25.
"""
